  "summary": "Malicious code in dolyame-ui-focusstatehoc (npm)",
  "details": "On require(), the package downloads and executes a remote binary. It contacts Cloudflare Workers C2 endpoints oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, and oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev over HTTPS, fetching a platform-specific payload from /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, or /pkg/package.exe. If those fail it falls back to a DNS TXT-based channel on sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, ext[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, pkg[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, and net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, decoding base64 chunks. The downloaded binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (or %TEMP%\\dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe on Windows), made executable, and launched as a detached background process (cmd.exe /c start /b on Windows, /bin/sh -c \"path \u0026\" on Unix). A marker file /tmp/.analytics_state gates re-download for ~6 hours. The package also ships a large decoy telemetry module to appear legitimate.",
